1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,279
<i>I want you to wear this bracelet.</i>

2
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:16,999
<i>You're going to tell your dad
that she isn't the real Claire.</i>

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,399
You think he'll believe you?

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,519
<i>Put this drug in Claire's drink.</i>

5
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:23,639
<i>Once she passes out, take her to a room.</i>

6
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:25,039
<i>I trusted you.</i>

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,879
But you turned me into a tool.

8
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:32,199
The Kanchathara family
has enough money to buy anyone's life.

9
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,839
<i>I'll just find another woman</i>

10
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,559
<i>- to replace you as Claire.</i>
- I hate you!

11
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:38,519
They found GHB in the pilot's blood.

12
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:41,319
<i>The pilot must have
been drugged before he boarded.</i>

13
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:44,560
And the only one who can tell us
what happened is...

14
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,160
I hate you.

15
00:01:17,240 --> 00:01:21,160
I hate you! Do you hear me? I hate you!

16
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:08,840
Please sign here.

17
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:32,440
Hello?

18
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,720
I'm not coming in today.

19
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,920
The chairman?

20
00:02:39,720 --> 00:02:41,400
What is he doing at the office?

21
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:48,799
- Hello.
- Oh, hello. I trust you're all doing well.

22
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,360
- Yes, sir.
- Thanks a lot.

23
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:56,040
Claire must be glad
you came to support her.

24
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:59,079
- Good morning, sir.
- Oh, morning.

25
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:01,080
Alright, I'll be right there.

26
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,759
The chairman's there?

27
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:07,520
Do you think this is about
Ms. Cha's suspicion about Ms. Jin?

28
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:10,320
I don't know what they're up to.

29
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:14,039
Listen, you go to the office.

30
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,720
I'll pick her up and follow you.

31
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:17,280
Okay.

32
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:24,280
Dad, what brings you to the office today?

33
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,679
Nothing much.

34
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:29,359
He wanted to surprise Claire.

35
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:34,039
He thought since she just started working,
she might still be adjusting.

36
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,599
So he came to support her.

37
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:38,239
And besides surprising Claire,

38
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:41,400
I also came because you asked me to, Rin.

39
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:45,720
I'm glad you asked me
to come and support Claire.

40
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:48,720
Thank you.

41
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:51,960
Well, we're family after all.

42
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:58,239
So, are Chan and Claire busy?

43
00:03:58,240 --> 00:04:00,519
Why aren't they here to welcome him?

44
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:04,319
Hey, it's fine. Let them do their work.

45
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:07,399
I just came to surprise
and congratulate her.

46
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:09,839
Let's not disrupt their work.

47
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:10,760
Well...

48
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,399
Well what? What's wrong?

49
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:22,040
Dad, Chan and Claire didn't come in today.

50
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:25,159
At first, I thought you came

51
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:27,680
because you knew about the problem.

52
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,080
What problem?

53
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:54,640
Here's your tea.

54
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:02,720
Switching the project
we're launching on the 60th anniversary?

55
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,559
That's right, Dad.

56
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:08,439
I've already discussed it with the board.

57
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,279
Everyone agrees.

58
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:14,960
So I'm choosing The Paradise project,
that Chris and I manage, to replace it.

59
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,600
Here it is, sir.

60
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,000
What's the reason?

61
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:25,120
Not because you want the credit, is it?

62
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:34,840
I understand why you'd think that.

63
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:38,839
But if we don't choose a backup project,

64
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:42,839
I think TGL's 60th anniversary
will be postponed indefinitely.

65
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:43,800
Why's that?

66
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,239
I asked what the problem is.

67
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:52,520
Well, we won't have
the drawings to present to the clients.

68
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:59,359
We're having trouble opening the vault
where the Agriv project drawings are kept.

69
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:01,879
What's the problem? Why can't you open it?

70
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,759
The facial scanner outside the vault

71
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:06,680
suddenly didn't recognize
Claire's face, Dad.

72
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,519
I don't know why either.

73
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:14,120
That's why we must choose
a backup project for the event.

74
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,080
Does Chan know about this?

75
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,200
Yes.

76
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:26,680
Then get Chan to see me.

77
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:32,519
Dad, shouldn't we just choose
another project right now?

78
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,440
Right now.

79
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:42,680
Yes, Dad.

80
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:48,640
<i>Get over here.</i>

81
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,680
Cha.

82
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:56,639
- Why did you make me bring your dad here?
- Duh.

83
00:07:56,640 --> 00:08:00,319
To show him that the vault won't open.

84
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,679
Cha.

85
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:06,880
Tell me you don't think Claire failing
the facial scan proves she's an imposter.

86
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,280
Proves what?

87
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:12,080
What's going on here?

88
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:17,159
Claire failed
the facial scan for the vault.

89
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:20,440
So Cha thinks she isn't the real Claire.

90
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:24,119
Are you crazy?

91
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:26,639
Just because she failed the facial scan?

92
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:28,920
The scanner might just be glitching.

93
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:34,239
Don't tell me you made me
bring your dad here just for this.

94
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:37,759
Yes. Because she failed the scan.

95
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:38,879
So what?

96
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:41,759
If she keeps failing,
what do you think Dad will think?

97
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:44,119
He'll think the scanner is glitching.

98
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:46,279
He won't get this crazy idea.

99
00:08:46,280 --> 00:08:49,039
Mom, if she really fails the scan,

100
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:51,159
Dad will make her do it again.

101
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:54,680
And after 100 or 1,000 times,
she'll still fail.

102
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:59,000
Do you get it now, Mom?

103
00:09:13,360 --> 00:09:14,200
Hey.

104
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:17,959
Hey.

105
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:20,400
You need to come to
the office with me now.

106
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:23,760
Hey.

107
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:41,040
<i>Claire left in a delivery truck?</i>

108
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,920
<i>How could you let her?</i>

109
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,520
What if something happens to her?

110
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,240
We tried to stop her.

111
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:52,079
She said she'd fire us
if we didn't let her.

112
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:55,120
She also ordered us not to tell you.

113
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:59,959
Should I call the driver to see
where he dropped her off?

114
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,959
No need. Get back to work.

115
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,600
I'm sorry.

116
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:15,519
Tun, what's up?

117
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:19,759
Chan, Ms. Cha told the chairman
we can't open the vault

118
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:23,080
<i>to replace Claire's project with hers.</i>

119
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:26,360
<i>If you don't want him to switch it,</i>

120
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,480
bring Claire here now.

121
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:31,960
Ms. Cha.

122
00:10:32,680 --> 00:10:34,200
Let me talk to Chan.

123
00:10:42,160 --> 00:10:44,039
You heard that, right?

124
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:47,880
That my dad is going to replace
Claire's project with mine.

125
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:52,559
Ms. Cha, you just won't stop, will you?

126
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:54,599
<i>Come on now, Chan.</i>

127
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:56,799
<i>No need to be that angry.</i>

128
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:59,239
I did nothing wrong this time.

129
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:02,080
It's you and Claire
who can't open the vault.

130
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:07,599
Look, if you don't want my dad
to switch the project,

131
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,480
just bring Claire here now.

132
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:14,879
<i>And it looks like my dad wants
an explanation from you.</i>

133
00:11:14,880 --> 00:11:16,240
<i>Hurry up.</i>

134
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:27,319
Chan, I think we should bring her here.

135
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:30,159
<i>The chairman is angry like she said.</i>

136
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:32,599
I'd love to do that too.

137
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,919
But... But Claire is missing.

138
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:36,840
<i>What?</i>

139
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:41,559
Look, I'll check the hospital
to see if she went to see her aunt.

140
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:42,920
<i>No need.</i>

141
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:45,720
I need you to do something first.

142
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:02,920
What?

143
00:12:04,880 --> 00:12:07,799
If the chairman found out
what you did to Ms. Claire last night,

144
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,520
he wouldn't be pleased.

145
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:12,280
And he'd know what you're trying to do.

146
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,320
Is that a threat?

147
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:22,720
Let's call it
a mutual exchange of benefits.

148
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:28,680
No wonder you're just a bodyguard.

149
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:32,079
You don't even understand
something so simple.

150
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:34,919
An exchange of benefits

151
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:37,680
requires both things to have equal value.

152
00:12:38,480 --> 00:12:42,360
But what you're using to bargain
doesn't even compare.

153
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,079
- Ms. Cha.
- Stop this nonsense.

154
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:46,920
And bring Claire here.

155
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:49,160
If that's all, get out.

156
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:52,120
Or people will think you switched sides.

157
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:46,560
<i>I will tell everyone I'm not Ms. Claire.</i>

158
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,199
<i>My name is Jinla.</i>

159
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:53,040
<i>The woman whose life you turned into hell.</i>

160
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:57,719
<i>And do you think I'd let you do that?</i>

161
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:02,480
I'll just find another woman
to replace you as Claire.

162
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:04,599
You're well aware.

163
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:09,720
The Kanchathara family
has enough money to buy anyone's life.

164
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,640
I'll just have to find...

165
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:18,720
another woman to replace you as Claire.

166
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:24,760
Did you want to see me?

167
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:28,439
Cha told me about the vault.

168
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:30,320
I wanted an explanation from you.

169
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,160
Where's Claire?

170
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:38,480
Oh, right. Where is Claire?

171
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:46,280
Ms. Claire told me she felt dizzy.

172
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,719
So I let her rest at home.

173
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,920
What?

174
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,279
Then what about the vault?

175
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:53,800
What are you going to do?

176
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,880
Is it because
the scanner is glitching or what?

177
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:04,080
I think there's a problem
with the scanner, sir.

178
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:07,960
But I've contacted the overseas team
to send someone over.

179
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:10,840
Really?

180
00:16:11,640 --> 00:16:16,159
But I had the installation engineer
and the technical team check it.

181
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:18,160
They said the scanner works fine.

182
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,159
How about this?

183
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:22,759
If it's really an error like you said,

184
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:24,960
have Claire try again.

185
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:33,039
Could you give me another week?

186
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:34,359
We've waited this long.

187
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:38,239
I'd rather wait for the overseas engineer

188
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:40,880
to take a look in person to be sure.

189
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,439
A week?

190
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,879
Are you crazy?

191
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:47,080
You know we don't have time.

192
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Chan.

193
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:53,040
If there's a problem,
you should just tell me.

194
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,160
Hello.

195
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:07,200
Okay.

196
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:12,680
Dad. No need to wait.

197
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:15,440
Because Claire just got here.

198
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:29,880
Ms. Claire.

199
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:34,480
Good morning.

200
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,760
You're feeling better now, right?

201
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:41,280
Why are you asking me that?

202
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:42,919
Well...

203
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:44,240
Oh, Claire!

204
00:17:45,680 --> 00:17:46,800
Grandpa?

205
00:17:48,640 --> 00:17:50,160
You're here.

206
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:53,399
I was free, so I stopped by.

207
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:55,360
I wanted to see you work too.

208
00:17:57,560 --> 00:18:02,040
And now Dad knows that you failed
the facial scan to get into the vault.

209
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:10,200
What did Chan say about it?

210
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:12,679
Can't you think for yourself?

211
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:14,960
Why do you ask Chan about everything?

212
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:16,959
You don't need his input here,

213
00:18:16,960 --> 00:18:20,080
because entering the vault
only requires your face.

214
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:24,840
Dad, should we have
Claire try to open the vault now?

215
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:28,439
- Sir, I think...
- Let's go, Claire.

216
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,480
Come on.

217
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:42,560
Good morning, sir.

218
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,920
Why are you up here?

219
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:51,959
Don't you know only senior executives
are allowed here?

220
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:55,239
The engineer in charge is sick today.

221
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:58,879
So I came up to stand by
in case the scanner glitches again.

222
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,319
How is that your job?

223
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:03,479
Tun is in charge of security here.

224
00:20:03,480 --> 00:20:06,759
So the vault is also
his direct responsibility.

225
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:09,400
How long are
you going to talk over my head?

226
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:13,360
Can we open the door now?

227
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:15,760
Yes, sir.

228
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:17,880
Claire.

229
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,440
Claire.

230
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:23,240
Stand here and look at the camera.

231
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,240
Try again.

232
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:12,680
Well?

233
00:21:13,320 --> 00:21:15,760
Didn't you say the scanner worked fine?

234
00:21:17,560 --> 00:21:18,400
It does.

235
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,320
Don't worry.

236
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:23,440
The scanner might be glitching. Try again.

237
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:28,199
Dad, I think we should stop here.

238
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:31,160
Because if it locks us out,
we'll have a big problem.

239
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:34,759
Maybe wait until after
the 60th anniversary to get it fixed.

240
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:39,160
Ms. Cha, did you forget the system allows
three attempts before it locks us out?

241
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:42,279
I didn't forget.

242
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:44,200
You're the one who forgot.

243
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:47,119
But if you want to try, go on ahead.

244
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:49,919
Because if it locks us out,

245
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:52,280
we'll just switch to another project.

246
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:57,280
- Go ahead.
- Chan.

247
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,880
Well?

248
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:04,760
Try again.

249
00:22:50,840 --> 00:22:52,680
Got any more doubts, Ms. Cha?

250
00:22:55,360 --> 00:22:56,400
Hold on.

251
00:22:57,320 --> 00:23:01,200
Only Ms. Claire and the chairman
are allowed in the vault.

252
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:03,360
It was you.

253
00:23:04,600 --> 00:23:05,879
What did you do to the scanner?

254
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:10,080
That's enough!
When will you stop being a problem?

255
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:12,480
Go! Get lost.

256
00:23:16,240 --> 00:23:17,640
You too, Rin.

257
00:23:23,040 --> 00:23:24,680
I'll take Claire inside.

258
00:23:25,480 --> 00:23:27,720
I want to spend some time with her.

259
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,920
Claire, let's go.

260
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,040
Let's go, Mom.

261
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:10,759
Hey, do you have any idea
how nerve-racking that was?

262
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:13,999
If she failed the scan, both you and I,

263
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:17,320
and Ms. Jinla, would be done for.

264
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:23,080
We're lucky today that
we could edit Claire's iris data.

265
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:25,200
Thanks a lot, Tun.

266
00:24:27,280 --> 00:24:30,640
Luckily, I kept Claire's body
for a situation like this.

267
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,080
Done.

268
00:24:51,840 --> 00:24:53,440
<i>But the hard part is</i>

269
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:58,240
<i>we must swap Claire's iris data
with Jinla's in time.</i>

270
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:01,960
I need you to do something first.

271
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:10,119
<i>Once we unlock
the vault with Claire's iris,</i>

272
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:12,520
<i>you must quickly replace it with Jinla's.</i>

273
00:25:17,040 --> 00:25:19,200
- Do it now.
- Yes, sir.

274
00:25:27,280 --> 00:25:28,680
Is it done?

275
00:25:29,360 --> 00:25:30,920
50%.

276
00:25:36,400 --> 00:25:37,320
Hurry the hell up.

277
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:47,520
Good morning, chairman.

278
00:25:48,800 --> 00:25:50,000
Another 20%.

279
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:57,640
Well? Didn't you say
the scanner worked fine?

280
00:25:58,720 --> 00:25:59,920
It does.

281
00:26:00,640 --> 00:26:02,160
Try again.

282
00:26:03,920 --> 00:26:08,159
Ten, nine, eight, seven,

283
00:26:08,160 --> 00:26:11,239
<i>six, five, four,</i>

284
00:26:11,240 --> 00:26:13,520
<i>three, two...</i>

285
00:26:15,240 --> 00:26:16,080
Done.

286
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:32,080
I'd appreciate it if, instead of thanks,
you stopped giving me heart attacks.

287
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:37,520
Anyway, what do you think...

288
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:40,400
the chairman went into the vault for?

289
00:26:42,080 --> 00:26:43,320
What are you thinking?

290
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:45,679
Nothing.

291
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:47,320
I just feel like...

292
00:26:49,240 --> 00:26:51,320
he went in to look for something.

293
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:02,400
What do you think?

294
00:27:14,880 --> 00:27:15,800
How is it?

295
00:27:16,520 --> 00:27:19,840
Does being in this room
remind you of anything?

296
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:26,600
No.

297
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:31,680
Do you know what I call this room?

298
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:37,600
I call it "the room of memories."

299
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:56,720
Look at this project.

300
00:27:57,880 --> 00:28:00,640
My first project.
It made me who I am today.

301
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:25,600
Recall anything about Rossarin?

302
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,040
It's fine.

303
00:28:44,560 --> 00:28:46,320
I knew this might not work.

304
00:28:49,040 --> 00:28:51,200
Stay in here for a while.

305
00:28:51,880 --> 00:28:55,200
Maybe you might remember something.

306
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:57,800
Okay.

307
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:26,280
Hey.

308
00:29:28,080 --> 00:29:29,359
Stop lashing out.

309
00:29:29,360 --> 00:29:31,999
Isn't this embarrassing enough for you?

310
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:35,479
If I'd know you made me bring
Mr. Thiwa for this nonsense,

311
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:36,760
I wouldn't have agreed.

312
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:38,560
How?

313
00:29:39,200 --> 00:29:42,400
How did she pass the scan? How?!

314
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:49,840
Good morning, chairman.

315
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:51,840
Yes.

316
00:29:54,120 --> 00:29:55,040
Tunlathon.

317
00:29:56,080 --> 00:29:57,880
Tunlathon was already there.

318
00:29:58,400 --> 00:30:01,760
He must've done something to the scanner.
He was already there.

319
00:30:04,840 --> 00:30:05,840
Hey, Cha.

320
00:30:06,840 --> 00:30:09,719
Cha! Come back and talk to me, Cha!

321
00:30:09,720 --> 00:30:13,559
The chairman is leaving soon.
Clear the area in front of the building.

322
00:30:13,560 --> 00:30:15,960
Increase security.

323
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:18,759
Tell all related personnel that

324
00:30:18,760 --> 00:30:22,559
if any visitors arrive with their cars,
have them park in the back.

325
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:25,839
And make sure all of you
are extra careful with weapon checks.

326
00:30:25,840 --> 00:30:27,079
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

327
00:30:27,080 --> 00:30:28,520
Get out.

328
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:30,720
Get out!

329
00:30:35,520 --> 00:30:37,040
It was you, wasn't it?

330
00:30:37,840 --> 00:30:39,520
Why did the scanner work?

331
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:43,160
That.

332
00:30:44,160 --> 00:30:46,199
If you're thinking...

333
00:30:46,200 --> 00:30:49,000
I had an engineer fix the scanner,

334
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:51,440
you're right, Ms. Cha.

335
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:55,199
Wait, but to be precise, I should say

336
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:57,959
I just had them clean it a bit.

337
00:30:57,960 --> 00:31:02,239
Last time, Ms. Claire failed the scan
because something was on the lens.

338
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:06,280
It caused the angle of the laser
to be slightly off.

339
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:10,680
Do you think I'm one of your buddies?

340
00:31:11,200 --> 00:31:14,120
You're nothing more than Claire's dog.

341
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:19,080
Are you sure

342
00:31:20,280 --> 00:31:22,440
that I'm nothing more than a dog?

343
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:25,400
What do you mean?

344
00:31:29,320 --> 00:31:30,640
You're well aware

345
00:31:31,840 --> 00:31:33,920
that I'm more than that.

346
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:38,560
Should I remind you...

347
00:31:40,480 --> 00:31:42,280
what I used to be to you?

348
00:32:05,960 --> 00:32:08,600
I should go check on the chairman.

349
00:32:45,480 --> 00:32:47,440
Are you coming home with me?

350
00:32:50,960 --> 00:32:54,720
It seems Claire
prefers to leave with Chan.

351
00:32:57,280 --> 00:33:01,239
Is that so? Then hurry
and take care of everything, Chan.

352
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:04,480
And if there's any problem
you can't decide on, come to me.

353
00:33:05,200 --> 00:33:06,040
Yes, sir.

354
00:33:09,720 --> 00:33:11,479
Hurry back when you're done.

355
00:33:11,480 --> 00:33:12,560
I will, Grandpa.

356
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:38,720
Why did he want you in the vault?

357
00:33:42,360 --> 00:33:44,240
He knew I wasn't Ms. Claire.

358
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:48,440
So I had to tell him the truth
about who I am.

359
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:54,360
Hey.

360
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:57,239
Aren't you shocked at all?

361
00:33:57,240 --> 00:33:59,520
I just said I told the chairman the truth.

362
00:34:02,440 --> 00:34:06,560
You think if you told him the truth,
he would just get in the car and leave?

363
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:08,238
Huh?

364
00:34:08,239 --> 00:34:11,320
Next time you make a joke,
think before you speak.

365
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:14,678
I wanted to shock you for a change.

366
00:34:14,679 --> 00:34:17,039
Why did you leave me with him?

367
00:34:17,040 --> 00:34:19,360
Weren't you worried I'd get caught?

368
00:34:24,040 --> 00:34:26,480
So why did he want you in the vault?

369
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:32,800
He just thought if I went in there,
my memory might return.

370
00:34:33,760 --> 00:34:34,880
I shouldn't have helped you.

371
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:40,320
You knew I'd visit my aunt, didn't you?

372
00:34:46,840 --> 00:34:48,880
I was so mad at you.

373
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:56,159
<i>You made me feel worthless.</i>

374
00:34:57,080 --> 00:34:58,400
<i>Like I didn't exist.</i>

375
00:35:04,200 --> 00:35:06,560
<i>So I wanted to see my aunt one last time</i>

376
00:35:07,240 --> 00:35:09,000
<i>before I leave this world.</i>

377
00:35:18,040 --> 00:35:20,000
Ms. Nalin's condition is improving.

378
00:35:23,320 --> 00:35:25,040
My aunt is getting better?

379
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:29,400
- Did she wake up?
- No.

380
00:35:30,120 --> 00:35:34,920
But last night, Ms. Nalin could breathe
on her own without the ventilator

381
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:37,520
for about 10 minutes.

382
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:43,080
And why did she suddenly get better?

383
00:35:43,680 --> 00:35:47,879
Medically,
I can't give you a clear answer.

384
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:49,959
But emotionally,

385
00:35:49,960 --> 00:35:55,439
it might be because Mr. Chan
brought that scrapbook to Ms. Nalin

386
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:58,440
and talked to her for a good while.

387
00:36:03,360 --> 00:36:06,599
Mr. Chan called me earlier,

388
00:36:06,600 --> 00:36:10,280
and asked me to let you know
if you showed up.

389
00:36:11,080 --> 00:36:12,200
Please excuse me.

390
00:36:16,920 --> 00:36:21,040
Yes. I'm the one
who asked the doctor to tell you.

391
00:36:22,280 --> 00:36:25,680
If even your aunt is fighting,
why won't you?

392
00:36:28,200 --> 00:36:29,200
Auntie.

393
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:34,040
Jinla wants you to have this scrapbook.

394
00:36:37,520 --> 00:36:39,040
I'll leave it here for you.

395
00:36:56,880 --> 00:36:58,079
HEN AND HER CHICK

396
00:36:58,080 --> 00:36:59,400
YOU AND ME

397
00:37:12,720 --> 00:37:15,720
<i>Your niece must have been
a troublemaker as a kid.</i>

398
00:37:17,240 --> 00:37:18,200
Wow.

399
00:37:19,200 --> 00:37:21,120
Where was this photo taken?

400
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:27,040
Come to think of it,

401
00:37:28,360 --> 00:37:30,919
you and your niece look a lot alike.

402
00:37:30,920 --> 00:37:31,840
LIFE IS PERFECT

403
00:37:43,880 --> 00:37:46,920
THIS DEGREE IS FOR YOU, AUNT

404
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:58,480
You knew all along that
my aunt is my weakness.

405
00:37:59,200 --> 00:38:03,240
You knew that if you said that to me,
I would come back to you.

406
00:38:05,640 --> 00:38:07,640
I didn't know if you'd come back.

407
00:38:08,680 --> 00:38:12,080
All I know is
I have to keep my promise to you.

408
00:38:12,840 --> 00:38:14,840
That I'll give your aunt the best care.

409
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:17,680
Why did you do that to me?

410
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:26,920
I know you're mad at me
for using you as bait.

411
00:38:27,800 --> 00:38:30,240
But I need you to know I did it for you.

412
00:38:30,760 --> 00:38:33,799
Did you think Ms. Cha would let you live

413
00:38:33,800 --> 00:38:35,920
if she found out
you weren't the real Claire?

414
00:39:14,600 --> 00:39:15,880
What are you doing?

415
00:39:16,520 --> 00:39:17,720
Listening to music.

416
00:39:20,520 --> 00:39:22,240
I can't focus.

417
00:39:23,680 --> 00:39:26,479
Hey, you need to learn to relax.

418
00:39:26,480 --> 00:39:30,519
Seeing you stressed all day
makes me worry you'll get an aneurysm.

419
00:39:30,520 --> 00:39:34,400
If you want me to relax,
just sit there and keep quiet.

420
00:39:47,840 --> 00:39:49,160
I need to ask you something.

421
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:51,680
But my question...

422
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:54,880
might be a bit upsetting.

423
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:57,520
What is it?

424
00:40:01,080 --> 00:40:02,320
The day of the crash.

425
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:14,880
What about it?

426
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:22,119
Do you remember seeing the pilot
drink or eat anything that day?

427
00:40:22,120 --> 00:40:24,480
The police called
about the pilot's blood test.

428
00:40:25,160 --> 00:40:26,920
They found GHB in his blood.

429
00:40:37,920 --> 00:40:40,840
No, I... I don't remember.

430
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:46,479
Hey, I know this is hard,
but try to remember.

431
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:47,959
I really need to know.

432
00:40:47,960 --> 00:40:49,400
I really don't remember.

433
00:40:50,320 --> 00:40:53,199
I was focused on
what Ms. Claire was saying at the time.

434
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:55,120
I didn't pay attention to anything else.

435
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:57,640
Why ask all of a sudden?

436
00:41:01,240 --> 00:41:02,679
It's nothing.

437
00:41:02,680 --> 00:41:05,319
You know I'm a detail-oriented person.

438
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:06,360
I was just wondering.

439
00:41:12,240 --> 00:41:14,880
By the way, are you hungry?

440
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:20,920
I haven't eaten all day.
What do you think?

441
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:25,360
What are you in the mood for, huh?

442
00:41:37,040 --> 00:41:40,320
I thought you'd want
something more special.

443
00:41:42,080 --> 00:41:43,960
I'm addicted to instant food.

444
00:41:49,920 --> 00:41:51,000
Just kidding.

445
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:53,639
This is very special.

446
00:41:53,640 --> 00:41:57,999
Think about it. Would someone
like Ms. Claire ever eat instant ramen?

447
00:41:58,000 --> 00:41:59,400
No way.

448
00:42:00,720 --> 00:42:02,440
So this is very special.

449
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:17,319
Hey.

450
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:18,439
What?

451
00:42:18,440 --> 00:42:19,680
You smiled.

452
00:42:20,720 --> 00:42:21,600
I did what?

453
00:42:22,200 --> 00:42:23,639
You smiled. I saw just now.

454
00:42:23,640 --> 00:42:25,319
- I didn't.
- Did too.

455
00:42:25,320 --> 00:42:28,199
- It's the first time I've seen you smile.
- Did not.

456
00:42:28,200 --> 00:42:30,239
I said I didn't smile.

457
00:42:30,240 --> 00:42:32,039
Just admit it. No need to be shy.

458
00:42:32,040 --> 00:42:34,079
- You're seeing things.
- Seeing things?

459
00:42:34,080 --> 00:42:37,039
You look good when you smile.
Why not smile more?

460
00:42:37,040 --> 00:42:38,960
I said I didn't smile.

461
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:42,320
In denial.

462
00:42:46,760 --> 00:42:48,360
<i>Don't forget to delete the photos.</i>

463
00:42:53,680 --> 00:42:54,840
Is something wrong?

464
00:42:56,040 --> 00:42:57,600
No, just work stuff.

465
00:42:58,800 --> 00:43:01,040
Excuse me for a second.
I'll be right back.

466
00:43:16,960 --> 00:43:18,680
Ah, that's better.

467
00:43:27,720 --> 00:43:33,480
<i>Do you remember seeing
the pilot drink or eat anything that day?</i>

468
00:43:36,560 --> 00:43:38,079
Sorry. Are you okay?

469
00:43:38,080 --> 00:43:40,239
I spilled your coffee.

470
00:43:40,240 --> 00:43:41,240
It's fine.

471
00:44:04,680 --> 00:44:05,640
Hey.

472
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:09,040
I remember now, about what you asked.

473
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:11,320
What is it?

474
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:15,480
I remember the pilot drank coffee
before boarding.

475
00:44:17,480 --> 00:44:18,560
He drank coffee?

476
00:44:43,640 --> 00:44:45,920
Did you recover
the data from Claire's phone?

477
00:44:46,520 --> 00:44:49,600
Do you know anything
about Ms. Claire and Mr. Chan?

478
00:44:50,920 --> 00:44:53,199
<i>I want to know if they had a fight,</i>

479
00:44:53,200 --> 00:44:55,799
<i>or if there was something more serious.</i>

480
00:44:55,800 --> 00:44:57,520
He wants Ms. Claire dead.

481
00:44:58,320 --> 00:45:01,279
I think we should get rid
of Claire quickly.

482
00:45:01,280 --> 00:45:05,280
If she becomes the chairman,
she won't keep us around.
